cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
title: "2D hydrogen atom and hydrogenic impurity: analytic solution and finite elements from scratch"
abstract: >-
  Analytic solution of the 2D Coulomb problem and an in-house P2
  finite-element solver (Delaunay mesh, sparse assembly, shift-invert
  eigensolver) for the hydrogen atom in vacuum and a hydrogenic donor in GaAs.
  Includes orbitals, validation tables and a COMSOL reference model.
authors:
  - family-names: Parra Parra
    given-names: Daniel
    email: sasukeda25@gmail.com
    affiliation: Universidad Industrial de Santander (UIS)
type: software
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/danielparra2/2d-hydrogen-atom-hydrogenic-impurity"
notes: >-
  Companion material of the BSc Physics thesis "Effect of a donor impurity on
  the optoelectronic properties of a linear quantum dot chain" (UIS, 2026,
  laureate thesis, grade 5.0).
keywords:
  - hydrogen atom
  - hydrogenic impurity
  - 2D Coulomb problem
  - finite element method
  - quadratic Lagrange elements
  - GaAs
  - scientific computing
